The separation metrics of dimensionality-reduction evaluation count each group once: the scaling, the fit and the balanced accuracy weight each sample by one over its group's size (the fit then balances the classes, with weights averaging 1 so regularisation keeps its scale), so a subject with many epochs no longer outweighs the others. With one sample per group the logistic-regression score is unchanged. The random forest uses 200 trees instead of 300, 1.5 times faster with the same scores within its seed-to-seed spread.
